Under `jinja: true` the three templatable step frontmatter fields — `summary:`, `detached:` and
`review_gate:` — are rendered through the context before the sections are built, so `one`'s
evaluated summary shows in both the step table and its section, its evaluated `detached:` picks the
named agent, and its evaluated `review_gate:` shows in the table and its delegation order.

`two` names a config key that does not exist: `detached:` renders to the empty string and the step
degrades to runner-performed — instruction bullets and a fetch line, no delegation sentence and no
agent with an empty name. Its `review_gate:` renders empty too, which means no gate at all.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  fx_agent: fx-runner
  fx_threshold: 7
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-fields/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-jinja-fields
title: Jinja Fields
summary: Step frontmatter rendered through the context.
jinja: true
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-fields/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  one: []
  two: [one]
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-fields/one/prompt.md --
---
name: one
summary: Split past {{ config.core.fx_threshold }} SP
detached: '{{ config.core.fx_agent }}'
review_gate: 'confirm past {{ config.core.fx_threshold }} SP'
---

One body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-jinja-fields/two/prompt.md --
---
name: two
summary: Plain summary.
detached: '{{ config.core.no_such_key }}'
review_gate: '{{ config.core.no_such_key }}'
---

Two body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-jinja-fields
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Preamble.

## Playbook Steps

Execute the steps in the most effective order considering their dependencies.

| Step | Dependencies | Summary | Review gate |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `one` | — | Split past 7 SP | confirm past 7 SP |
| `two` | `one` | Plain summary. | — |

## Step: One

Split past 7 SP

Review gate: stop after this step — "confirm past 7 SP"; continue only on explicit user confirmation.

Tell the `fx-runner` agent to get its instructions by calling this command: `booping render-playbook fx-jinja-fields --step one`.

## Step: Two
Instructions:
- Summary: Plain summary.
- After: one

Run `booping render-playbook fx-jinja-fields --step two` for content.
